  "body": "Both this  methods don't modificate tokens so probably should have similar behavior when `token` argument has empty string and ASCII whitespace. Currently `contains()` throw (like all other DOMTokenList methods) and `supports()` doesn't throw. So there is two solution:\n- change `supports()` to throwing, this method is new so compatibility should not be a problem.\n- change `contains()` to not throwing because in this scenerio it's unnecessary (we don't change tokens) so we get little simplification.\n\nBTW:\nStep 2. and 3. in \"validation steps\" (https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-domtokenlist-validation) probably can be replace by one step. I don't see that you copy passing argument to new variable for any other methods that operate on argument converted to ASCII lowercase:\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-createelement\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-document-createattribute\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-attributes-get-by-name\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-element-setattribute\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-element-hasattribute \nbut not sure which style is more correct.\n",
